{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552343-what-attracted-you-to-vtm","id":1552343,"title":"What attracted you to VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-13T21:19:00-07:00","id":1552343,"title":"What attracted you to VTM?","content":"I got intrigued by a series of Mick Farren novels that focused on a coven of undead led by a thousand year old vampire by the Victor Renquist and how they reside along side humans and influence people or organizations when they need to. This series made me interested if this was ever done in a rpg game and thus I discovered VTM.<br /> <br /> So how did you discover the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T09:07:22-07:00","id":1552373,"title":"","content":"VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE - REDEMPTION.<br /> <br /> No, really, it\u2019s that simple (and I no longer have any idea what persuaded me to buy or ask for that game in the first place, it was so long ago).<br /> <br /> <br /> Technically speaking, it was the said video game that introduced me to the Masquerade, but it was WEREWOLF THE WILD WEST (No \u2018y\u2019 at that point) that really got me hooked on the World of Darkness, but I remembered REDEMPTION fondly enough to also take a second look at MASQUERADE thereafter (Specifically DARK AGES: VAMPIRE).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T10:41:59-07:00","id":1552377,"title":"","content":"I learned about the games when reading about RPGs in general, it was quite popular at the time, even more than D&amp;D. It was by the second half of the 90's. Anyone in the hobby by then would learn about the World of Darkness sooner or later, probably sooner, regardless of interest.<br /> <br /> And what attracted me, besides it being popular, is simply that I like vampires, always had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T11:28:01-07:00","id":1552380,"title":"","content":"I believe I've told this story a few times around here:<br /> <br /> My first TTRPG was the old WEG Star Wars, which I played because I was a massive Star Wars fan. Our GM wanted to try out VtM, and we went along with it. While I have played in VtM games here and there over the decades, VtM served more as a stepping stone to other WoD games for me (or occasionally the game I used to introduce others as it was the most well known and one of the more approachable ones for those that don't know the WoD) rather than one of my core games to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T13:10:19-07:00","id":1552389,"title":"","content":"I just thought it looked cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T13:35:39-07:00","id":1552391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552343-what-attracted-you-to-vtm?p=1552389#post1552389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought it looked cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I felt about the Mokole and Rokea when I saw the W:tA player's guide post-play session of Vampire. Which followed on the heels of exposure to KtE and VTES, though the other people in my group had been talking about it for years by then. The call of werereptiles and weresharks got me to switch over like lightning, and I grew to not like looking back (quieted after the 20th anniversary edition, aggravated to an inner furnace after W5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T16:30:12-07:00","id":1552429,"title":"","content":"I attended a gaming con in early 90's and there was a live action game called Vampire; I was intrigued but had no idea what it was. I showed up was given a character (Gangrel) and told I was an Anarch who was fighting the oppression of the elders. 3 hours later I was hooked. Crazy thing was I didn't play again until late 90's when the tv show Kindred the Embraced came out and VtM started catching on. I have played ever since. (A gap here and there but pretty much my number #1 game) <br /> <br /> PS I have yet to try V5, currently running a V20-Chicago by Night (set in early 2000) and Milwaukee by Night V20 (set in the same time frame)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T06:46:30-07:00","id":1552487,"title":"","content":"How much llore and background there was. I then came to realize that much of this lore and background didn't really work for the kind of games I most enjoyed but it was still what brought me in and what keeps me interested in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-17T09:32:31-07:00","id":1552493,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">I remember when I saw <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> (first edition) in a local game shop back in '91. I flipped through it and oh my! Did I <i>HATE</i> it! It looked like they'd made un-dead monsters into <b>D&amp;D</b> classes, the 'sooper powerz' (Disciplines and blood magic) looked simplistic, and the art did nothing for me... Fast forward a year-or-so, and a mate lent me his <b>Second Edition</b> book. I had terrible insomnia and decided that I'd read through it to find <i>EXACTLY</i> why it was bollocks. <br /> <br /> Um, needless to say that once I actually <i>READ</i> it, I fell in love. I spent all night poring over that book, and then the next day I did the same, and then I started writing notes, and well. All this time since I've been building my own world (of Darkness) for myself and \u2014 when they can attend \u2014 my friends, using that baseline that I loved.<br /> <br /> What I found most intriguing was the deep history element. I'm not a huge fan of the <i>Book of Nod</i> as THE HISTORY OF THE KINDRED. Rather, I'm fascintaed that there is scholarship into the mytho-historic origins of the Damned. The mechanic of Generation and the implication that it all started somewhere in the unknowable past \u2014 something that even 'immortal' monsters cannot know \u2014 lit a fire in me. The idea of the <i>Book of Nod</i> as a discrete artefact grew into it being more a collection of somewhat-related pieces, and some of the Damned see it as all nonsense whilst others believe it to be (no quotation marks) canon. That is, no two Kindred or Cainites or what-have-you can agree on their origins, and that fact makes their war of the ages so, so personal AND far away at the same time. The clans and bloodlines grow out of this set of disagreements, and those lines in turn force the drawing of other lines. For the trench coated neonate with her naff katana on the rain-soaked streets of wherever, the Jyhad is always part of the night she struggles through without any real understanding of why.<br /> <br /> A lot of the above has grown in my head over the past decades, mind you. I mean, it's all there in the very first book (which I do not own and adore), and it finds its way through all of the editions. It's filtered differently in Revised versus V5, but it still exists. The long arm of history-based-on-memory, it is a core precept that I found irresistible. It's a big part of why I have a Beckett action figure on my desk and own the <b>Book of Nod Artefact Edition </b>and my players know the name 'Bindusara' as blood-sucking scholar of the supernatural rather than an emperor in Indian history. There are MANY other points in the game that I find wonderful, but I believe this is what first made me excited.<br /> <br /> The TL;DR version: First attracted by spite. Eh... But it got better? </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-19T05:02:26-07:00","id":1552526,"title":"","content":"The setting and the canon story.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}